&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Director of Product Marketing at Storyblok, We&#39;re looking for a Product Marketing Director to shape how we position, launch, and grow our product in the market- particularly in the US, UK and EMEA. This is a senior, hands-on role for someone who can translate complex technical capability into compelling, credible narratives — and who&#39;s comfortable in the room with engineers as much as with executives. You&#39;ll own the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, Sales, and Marketing at a stage where positioning decisions have outsized impact on growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will guide a talented team, focusing on sales enablement, website conversion, feature adoption, and Storyblok’s market positioning with industry analysts and customer review platforms. A key responsibility is to elevate our product marketing function to influence revenue, customer acquisition, and market leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission is to enable Storyblok to win in the market by clearly articulating our value, differentiation, and future direction.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re genuinely comfortable operating in technical territory, not just translating it secondhand. You can read API documentation, understand headless CMS architecture, and hold a credible, detailed conversation with engineers and technical evaluators about how the product actually works — its components, integration points, and trade-offs versus alternative approaches. This fluency shows up in the quality of your messaging: you write positioning that developers trust because it&#39;s accurate, not just persuasive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ve likely worked hands-on with developers before, whether as a technical product marketer, solutions engineer, technical product manager, or in an engineering-adjacent role, and you know how to earn credibility with a technical audience rather than assume it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Positioning &amp;amp; Messaging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve our core messaging and differentiated value proposition across all audiences (developers, marketers, partners, enterprise buyers), setting the strategic framework the wider team executes against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct ongoing customer, market, and competitive research programs to ensure messaging stays relevant, differentiated, and current&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standard for translating product capabilities and roadmap into solution-oriented, benefits-led messaging that resonates across the buyer journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure messaging consistency and governance across all channels — website, campaigns, sales assets, analyst briefings, and customer communications&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-To-Market Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own GTM strategy for major product and feature launches, driving alignment across Product, Growth, Sales, Customer Success, and Content leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define phased rollout strategies that drive awareness, adoption, and revenue impact across key customer segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standard for launch toolkits — messaging frameworks, FAQs, competitive positioning, product one-pagers, internal training — and build the team capability to produce them at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the measurement framework for launch performance and adoption, using it to continuously improve release execution&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Enablement &amp;amp; Sales Plays&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a structured sales playbook program aligned to product capabilities, customer pain points, and vertical use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip revenue teams with high-impact content (battlecards, ROI calculators, solution briefs, demo scripts, objection handling).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with Sales Leadership on rep onboarding, conversion effectiveness, and keeping messaging aligned to evolving sales motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use sales performance data, win/loss interviews, and customer feedback to identify and prioritize enablement investments&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyst &amp;amp; Review Site Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead the analyst relations strategy to secure meaningful participation in key analyst evaluations (e.g., Gartner Magic Quadrant, Forrester Wave, IDC MarketScape).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate analyst briefing cycles, submission processes, and relationships that enhance Storyblok’s visibility and influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our presence and growth strategy on review platforms (G2, Gartner Peer Insights), including review acquisition and profile optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish ongoing monitoring and response mechanisms for public reviews and rankings&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Website &amp;amp; CRO Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Growth Marketing and Web leadership to ensure product positioning is clearly and consistently represented site-wide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set priorities for CRO initiatives that improve engagement, conversion, and self-serve funnel performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define messaging strategy and success metrics for key product pages, feature highlights, and trial flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct ongoing testing and optimization of messaging, CTAs, layouts, and journey flows based on data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead, mentor, and inspire the Product Marketing team to deliver high-impact outcomes aligned with company goals.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team structure, priorities, and ways of working in partnership with marketing leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the team on messaging craft, technical fluency, and cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of ownership, curiosity, experimentation, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop individual growth plans, conduct regular performance reviews, and ensure team members have access to relevant coaching and training opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong collaboration across Product, Growth, Brand, and Sales teams to drive alignment and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in Product Marketing, with at least 2+ years in a leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a fast-growing B2B SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PLG motions, SaaS business models, and the product lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in GTM execution, analyst engagement, and pricing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills and executive presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in cross-functional collaboration and stakeholder influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with tools like Salesforce, Marketing Automation, G2, and PMM platforms (e.g., Klue) a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
